 "title": "-ma words are masculine, sentir, getting lost (me he perdido)",
 "cards": [
  {
   "title": "Recap: haber",
   "body": "he, hemos · ha, has, han.",
   "t": 0
  },
  {
   "title": "-ma words are masculine",
   "body": "Most -a words are feminine, but a small group ending in -ma are masculine: el problema. A very common learner error is 'la problema'.",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "the problem",
     "es": "el problema"
    },
    {
     "en": "Have you (formal) understood the problem?",
     "es": "¿Ha entendido el problema?"
    }
   ],
   "t": 38.8
  },
  {
   "title": "Why: they came from Greek",
   "body": "These words were neuter in Greek, and Greek neuter words look like masculine ones, so they were taken as masculine. If it ends in -ma, it's probably Greek and masculine.",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "the system",
     "es": "el sistema"
    },
    {
     "en": "Have you understood the system?",
     "es": "¿Has entendido el sistema?"
    }
   ],
   "t": 103.6
  },
  {
   "title": "sentir = to feel (and to smell)",
   "body": "Related to 'sensation'. It can also mean 'perceive', for example a smell.",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "Have you smelt the aroma?",
     "es": "¿Has sentido el aroma?"
    },
    {
     "en": "the programme / the climate",
     "es": "el programa / el clima"
    }
   ],
   "t": 172.4
  },
  {
   "title": "Getting lost = losing yourself",
   "body": "Spanish doesn't say 'get lost / get ready'; it says 'lose myself', 'ready myself'. In speech the two e's of me he blend together.",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "I've got lost.",
     "es": "Me he perdido."
    },
    {
     "en": "I'VE got lost.",
     "es": "Yo me he perdido."
    }
   ],
   "t": 252.3
  },
  {
   "title": "te = you / yourself; nos = us / ourselves",
   "body": "",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "You've got lost.",
     "es": "(Tú) te has perdido."
    },
    {
     "en": "We've lost it.",
     "es": "Lo hemos perdido."
    },
    {
     "en": "We've got lost.",
     "es": "(Nosotros) nos hemos perdido."
    }
   ],
   "t": 344.1
  }
 ],
